.TH NPP 1 "November 2026" "Neko++ 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
npp \- a GPU-rendered text editor in the shape of Notepad++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B npp
.RI [ switches ]
.RI [ file " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Neko++
is a text editor for Linux that reproduces Notepad++'s feature set: tabs,
syntax highlighting, regular-expression search, find in files, bookmarks,
macros, a function list, a folder panel, user-defined languages and a
WebAssembly plugin host.
.PP
It draws through wgpu, so it uses Vulkan when the machine has it, OpenGL when
it does not, and a software rasteriser when it has neither.
.PP
A file named
.B \-
is read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-instance
Start a second process even when one is already running. Without this, a
second invocation hands its files to the running editor and exits.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait
Block until every named document is closed. This is what makes the editor
usable as
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-line " \fIline\fR"
Put the caret on this line. Lines are counted from one, as a compiler error
counts them.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-column " \fIcolumn\fR"
Put the caret on this column, counted from one.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-software
Draw with the software rasteriser instead of the GPU. Useful over a remote
display, or when the driver is the problem.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/npp/settings.txt
Settings, one
.I key value
pair per line. Written by the Preferences dialog.
.TP
.I ~/.config/npp/
Session, recent files, macros, user-defined languages and installed plugins.
.PP
A configuration directory left behind under the old name,
.IR ~/.config/npp-rs/ ,
is moved to
.I ~/.config/npp/
the first time the program runs.
